\begin{center}
{
\Large
Operators and Decorators Quiz Practice Problems
}
\end{center}

\begin{note}
There are three ways to attach behavior to a class in python:
you can hand-write the dunder method that python calls,
you can use a class decorator to generate the dunder method for you,
or you can inherit the method from a parent class.
In this notes packet we study all three,
and we show how the built-in decorators \lstinline{@dataclass} and \lstinline{@total_ordering}
are just class decorators that generate dunders.
\end{note}
